INT. CAROUSEL WORKSHOP - NIGHT

Painted horses hang from chains. Gilded poles. A calliope under a tarp. Dust in lamplight.

KALINDA RUSSO (30s, black jumpsuit, tool roll) crouches at a floor panel. OSCAR TREMBLAY (50s, ex-clockmaker, magnifier on one eye) holds a flashlight steady. MOSES BELLAMY (20s, lookout, earbud) hovers by the door.

KALINDA
Pry bar.

Oscar hands it over. She slides the bar under the panel. Wood groans. A compartment opens. Inside, a velvet satchel.

OSCAR
There she is.

MOSES
(whispering)
Guys. Headlights.

Both freeze. A white beam sweeps the window, slides across the horses, and passes on.

KALINDA
(exhaling)
Keep breathing.

MOSES
I am breathing!

OSCAR
Quietly.

Kalinda lifts the satchel. Weighs it in her palm. Frowns.

KALINDA
Light.

OSCAR
What?

KALINDA
It's too light.

She opens it. Inside lies a single brass key and a note. Oscar reads over her shoulder.

OSCAR
"Try the horse."

KALINDA
^"Try the third horse."

They speak the same line at the same instant. Moses stares from one to the other.

MOSES
What third horse?

All three turn. Above them, a carousel horse with a chipped blue mane. Kalinda climbs onto the platform. Oscar follows. Moses bolts after. They gather around the animal, and she turns the key in a hidden lock at the saddle. The belly pops open. Gold coins pour into her arms.

A siren starts up outside.

MOSES
Oh no.

OSCAR
Oh yes.

They scatter. Moses dives under the calliope tarp. Oscar slides behind a stack of poles. Kalinda leaps from the platform, hugging the coins, and vanishes between two rows of horses as the doors burst open.
